.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project specific
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
# Any file actually holding keys. The tracked cybertrace/api_key_registry.py is
# only a loader — it reads os.getenv and stores nothing.
api_keys.py

# OSINT output files. Scratch run output stays out of the repo.
# evidence/ and runs/ are NOT tracked today — the negation below is deliberately
# left off, so nothing scraped off a market gets published by an absent-minded
# `git add .`. Flip it only after reading every run you are about to publish:
# the saved --save JSON is the corpus the extractor-precision audit measures
# against, so versioning it is the only way the numbers stay reproducible.
output/
outputs/
results/
reports/
*.json.out
*.json
# !evidence/*.json
*.report

# Investigation runs. runs/raw holds saved `search --save` JSON, runs/corpora
# holds the .db + .html a `correlate --db --html` writes. Both are regenerable
# from the raw JSON, and the HTML is a ~700KB pyvis dump — keep it out of git.
# runs/README.md is the tracked index: what each run is and why it was kept.
# `runs/*` not `runs/` — git never descends into an excluded directory, so the
# negation below only works if the contents are what is excluded.
runs/*
!runs/README.md

# Sensitive files — extra safety net
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml
config.local.py

# Tor
*.onion_cache

# External research datasets (Elliptic++, Evolution marketplace, DUTA-10K, ...).
# Only original/ is excluded, not external_data/ itself — same runs/README.md
# pattern as the runs/* block above. The payloads are multi-hundred-MB to
# multi-GB third-party archives with their own licenses, some UNKNOWN/unstated
# (Elliptic++), and never enter git history; manifest.json beside each
# original/ dir stays tracked — it's provenance metadata, not the dataset.
external_data/*/original/
# The blanket *.json rule above (line 78) would otherwise catch these too —
# same negation shape as !runs/README.md, needed for the same reason.
!external_data/*/manifest.json
